      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While I don't necessarily agree with this exact implementation I do agree that VRChat could implement something to help mitigate situations like this. Blocking feels very different from normal socials on a platform like this and I think it needs to be accounted for.\n\nPerhaps an optional notification upon joining that there's a blocked user in your instance, or listed on the instance details? Or maybe subtly warning you that you're standing too close to a blocked user, or talking over them? Without saying who it is of course. Something along those lines.\n\nI think it'd be much more elegant for the VRChat team to explore ways of unintrusively warning the player situations like this might be about to happen rather than giving you the tools to watch out for it yourself.\n\nWhile I understand the reasoning behind wanting to see the blocked user directly, I think this causes way too many possible ins for harassment that others have already pointed out. It just doesn't seem worth it to mess with the current blocking system considering you might as well just hide their avatar + mute them to get pretty much the same \"partially blocked\" result.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
